    "message": "Create server forks in a worker process\n\nThe server's fork and intervention apply checked their inputs and then\nrestored, captured and saved the child inside the HTTP request, so the\nsingle-threaded server answered nothing else for the whole fork (about 15 s\nat 1440 minutes). They now start a worker process like a computation and\nreturn at once; the Run is running until the child exists, and the run's\nlast_fork carries the outcome. The server restores the Run's status after\nrecording it. The project screen waits for the child and shows a failure.\nTests and the CLI still fork in the caller.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
